  "term": "organ",
  "says": "A tonewheel organ: sine tones at the drawbar footages stacked on the played note - 16' an octave below, 8' the note, 5 1/3' a fifth above, 4' an octave above - each a steady sine, no envelope to speak of (the key is a switch: instant on, instant off), no velocity, no vibrato unless a Leslie is added. Signature: a harmonic, steady tone with a flat level over the held note, an attack and a release both near zero, no noise, no stereo width of its own.",
